From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:13:21 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 47/48] gpiomem: true wording for prepare(), two recovery
 commands, rewrapped comment

prepare() runs before any pin is driven or changed (the constructors have
already requested or read lines, so "before anything is read" was too much).
The destructor's recovery now prints two commands, the bus lines first and
then CRESET_B, because pinctrl applies a list in ascending order and a
single list could release CRESET_B first; then pinctrl get for CDONE. The
comment above SCK_PHASE_NS is rewrapped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JG8Wtod8kFmcquwN34pFCa
